venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log

# The hand landmarker model, copied from the Android repo's
# app/src/main/assets/hand_landmarker.task.
#
# This WAS ignored, to avoid two copies of the same asset drifting apart.
# That turned out to be the wrong trade: PRIVACY_MODE defaults to
# "landmarks", which is the most model-dependent mode, so a fresh clone
# killed the node at startup (HandDetector raises FileNotFoundError ->
# SystemExit before a socket is ever opened) and landmark mode looked
# simply "not implemented". The cost of the drift risk is one byte-identical
# 7.8 MB file; the cost of the ignore was an unusable clone.
#
# The two copies are byte-for-byte identical (verified with fc /b,
# 7,819,105 bytes). Re-copy and re-verify if the Android hub's model changes.
#
# Everything else under models/ stays untracked: selfie_segmenter.tflite is
# only needed for PI_NODE_PRIVACY=segment, and is not a default path.
models/*
!models/hand_landmarker.task

# Offline test scripts and their artifacts. Development aids, not shipped
# code, so they stay untracked. The scripts resolve their paths relative to
# their own location, so they work no matter where they are invoked from.
test/
test_hand_photo.jpg
crop_debug_*.png
scene_debug.png
